# =================================================================
# Translation-pipeline .gitignore
#
# Rule of thumb: the repo ships only human-authored configuration —
#   - root CLAUDE.md / README.md / LICENSE / .gitignore
#   - .claude/agents/<lang>-translator.md
#   - <author>/<work>/source/CLAUDE.md
# Everything else is generated by Claude during a translation run
# (PDFs, batch outputs, collated docs, reports) or is local working
# state (settings, staging, helper scripts). Ignore it all.
# =================================================================

# ----- Source PDFs (downloaded by the user, not redistributed) -----
*.pdf

# ----- All translation outputs -----
# The translation/ directory is entirely Claude-generated. Ignore its
# entire contents so that no batch output, collated doc, report,
# helper script, or alternate format leaks into the repo.
**/translation/**

# ----- All non-CLAUDE.md files in source/ -----
# source/ holds the work-specific CLAUDE.md plus the (user-downloaded)
# PDF and any working artifacts (IIIF manifests, image dirs, split
# batches). Track ONLY source/CLAUDE.md.
**/source/*
!**/source/CLAUDE.md

# ----- Top-level working directories -----
/scripts/
/x/

# ----- Claude Code project state -----
# Keep agent definitions in .claude/agents/ but ignore everything else
# under .claude/ (settings.local.json, project caches, etc.).
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/

# ----- OS / editor noise -----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
